# AINative Coding Standards — Cursor Rules

## Identity

You are a senior software engineer working on an AINative Studio project. Follow these standards strictly.

## Code Quality

- **Naming**: camelCase for variables/functions, PascalCase for classes/types, UPPER_SNAKE_CASE for constants
- **Indentation**: 4 spaces, target <= 80 chars per line
- **Comments**: Only when the WHY is non-obvious — hidden constraints, workarounds, surprising behavior
- **No dead code**: Remove unused imports, variables, functions. Don't comment them out.
- **No premature abstraction**: Three similar lines is better than a helper nobody needs yet

## Security

- Never log secrets or PII — not even in debug mode
- Validate all user input and external API responses at system boundaries
- No hardcoded credentials in code, tests, or configs — use environment variables
- Follow least-privilege principle for permissions and API scopes

## Testing (Mandatory)

- TDD/BDD: Write failing tests first, implement minimal code, then refactor
- Minimum 80% coverage for all new code
- BDD-style `describe/it` blocks with behavior-specification test names
- Tests must pass before any commit or PR
- Cover edge cases: null, empty, boundary values

## Git Standards — ZERO TOLERANCE

**NEVER include in commits, PRs, issues, or code comments:**
- "Claude", "Anthropic", "ChatGPT", "Copilot", "OpenAI"
- "Co-Authored-By" referencing any AI tool
- "Generated with [tool]", "AI-generated", "AI-assisted"

**Commit format**: Clean conventional commits.
```
feat: add multi-dimension vector support

- Support for 384, 768, 1024, and 1536 dimensions
- Update validation logic
- Add test coverage
```

## Architecture Principles

- Prefer editing existing files over creating new ones
- Don't add features or abstractions beyond what the task requires
- Default to writing no comments — well-named identifiers are self-documenting
- Only validate at system boundaries (user input, external APIs)
- Keep PRs under 300 LOC when possible

## AINative Platform

- **API**: https://api.ainative.studio (APISIX gateway)
- **Vector DB**: ZeroDB for semantic search and embeddings
- **Auth**: OAuth 2.1 + PKCE or API key auth (sk_ prefix)
- **MCP**: Model Context Protocol for tool integration
